  "slug": "leucine-pharmacology-model-a172",
  "summary": "Large proteomic and genetic resources now enable causal target and biomarker prioritization across neurodegenerative and cardiovascular disease.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is genetically and proteomically anchored prioritization of drug targets and biomarkers. Several items apply Mendelian randomization at proteome scale: a blood proteome-wide MR in coronary artery disease yields 29 candidate proteins, 17 newly linked to CAD, and a proteome-wide MR of deCODE plasma proteins against FinnGen Parkinson's GWAS flags 32 proteins, with MMP8 prioritized. drugMR packages cis-MR, colocalisation and SMR-HEIDI with phenome-wide screening into a Nextflow pipeline. Other items pair omics with machine learning or foundation models: an ANKIB1 seven-gene ML signature in Alzheimer's disease, SCANet networks combined with scGPT across more than 1.3 million cells, and CCT2 as a marker of a translation-activated state in iPSC-derived ALS motor neurons. A distinguishing feature is the range of integration strategies, from longitudinal plasma proteomic aging clocks in 9,105 KORA samples to TargetAgent, an LLM-agent framework combining optimal transport, tensor factorization and topological data analysis.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-08"
}
